---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **한국 팀을 «무엇으로» 찾아보나. 그리고 그것이 나이를 말해 주나.** (`/desktop-or-phone`)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 지면인가 ────────────────────────────────────────────
 * 오늘 씨앗(구글뉴스 kpop 영문): 「K-pop's new power fans? Middle-aged Americans with
 * money and time to spend」
 *   ⛔ 우리는 나이를 못 잰다. 위키미디어는 나이를 안 준다.
 *   ✅ 기기는 준다. 그래서 기기를 재고, **기기가 나이를 말해 주지 «않는»다는 것까지 잰다.**
 *
 * ⭐ 답이 「평평하다」인 것이 이 지면의 값이다. 40년 데뷔 차이에도 3점 안이다.
 *   우리 강령 — 「재 보고 안 된다고 적는 것도 결과다.」
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 하지 않는 것 ─────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ 🔴 기기를 나이로 바꿔 쓰지 않는다. 씨앗이 나이 이야기였으니 여기서 미끄러지기 쉽다
 * ⛔ 「전화로 읽으면 어리다」·「컴퓨터로 읽으면 나이 들었다」를 안 쓴다 — 잰 것이 아니다
 * ⛔ 위쪽·아래쪽 극단만 보여 주고 「이 팀은 이렇다」로 안 쓴다 — 그 자리는 팀이 작아 잡음이다
 * ⛔ 못 잰 8팀을 0 으로 안 채운다
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import d from '../../data/kcw-device-split.json';

const TITLE = 'Desktop or phone: what people use to look up a Korean act, and why it is not a proxy for age';

const 셈 = d.셈;
/* ⭐ 지면이 «셀 때마다 다시 센다». 손으로 적어 두면 자료가 바뀔 때 지면이 자기와 싸운다 */
const 볼띠 = d.띠별.filter((b) => b.팀수 >= 10);
const 띠값 = 볼띠.map((b) => b.데스크톱몫중앙값).filter((v) => v !== null);
const 띠폭 = 띠값.length >= 2 ? Math.max(...띠값) - Math.min(...띠값) : null;
const 가장높은띠 = 볼띠.length ? 볼띠.reduce((a, b) => (b.데스크톱몫중앙값 > a.데스크톱몫중앙값 ? b : a)) : null;
const 가장낮은띠 = 볼띠.length ? 볼띠.reduce((a, b) => (b.데스크톱몫중앙값 < a.데스크톱몫중앙값 ? b : a)) : null;
const 작은띠 = d.띠별.filter((b) => b.팀수 > 0 && b.팀수 < 10);

/* 🔴 극단은 «작은 팀»이 차지한다. 그것을 그냥 보여 주면 손님이 팀 이야기로 읽는다.
   그래서 많이 읽히는 팀만 남기고 다시 세서 «그래도 평평한가»를 함께 낸다. */
const 많이읽힌선 = 100000;
const 많이읽힌 = d.팀.filter((t) => t.전체 >= 많이읽힌선);
const 중앙 = (a) => {
  const v = a.filter((x) => Number.isFinite(x)).sort((x, y) => x - y);
  if (!v.length) return null;
  const i = Math.floor((v.length - 1) / 2); const k = Math.ceil((v.length - 1) / 2);
  return (v[i] + v[k]) / 2;
};
const 많이읽힌중앙 = 중앙(많이읽힌.map((t) => t.데스크톱몫));
const 많이읽힌띠 = [...new Set(많이읽힌.map((t) => t.띠).filter(Boolean))].sort()
  .map((b) => { const 것 = 많이읽힌.filter((t) => t.띠 === b); return { 띠: b, 팀수: 것.length, 중앙: 중앙(것.map((t) => t.데스크톱몫)) }; })
  .filter((x) => x.팀수 >= 5);
const 많이읽힌띠값 = 많이읽힌띠.map((x) => x.중앙).filter((v) => v !== null);
const 많이읽힌폭 = 많이읽힌띠값.length >= 2 ? Math.max(...많이읽힌띠값) - Math.min(...많이읽힌띠값) : null;

const 몫 = (v) => (v == null ? 'not measured' : `${(Number(v) * 100).toFixed(1)}%`);
const 점 = (v) => (v == null ? 'not measured' : `${(Number(v) * 100).toFixed(1)} points`);
const 수 = (n) => (n == null ? '—' : Math.round(Number(n)).toLocaleString('en-US'));
const 위키 = (t) => `https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/${encodeURIComponent(String(t).split(' ').join('_'))}`;

const DESC =
  `We measured which device ${수(셈.잰팀수)} Korean acts are looked up on — English Wikipedia, `
  + `${d.창}. Desktop is ${몫(셈.합쳐본데스크톱몫)} of all reading and ${몫(셈.데스크톱몫중앙값)} for `
  + `the median act, and it barely moves with debut era: ${점(띠폭)} across four decades. So device `
  + 'is not a stand-in for how old the audience is.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: d.창,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/', 'https://query.wikidata.org/'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} page="/desktop-or-phone" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <h1>Desktop or phone: what people use to look up a Korean act</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    An English-language piece this week asked whether K-pop's new power fans are
    middle-aged Americans with money and time to spend. We cannot answer that. Wikimedia
    publishes no reader age, and nothing on this page is a claim about how old anybody is.
    What Wikimedia does publish is the <b>device</b>, and the reason to put it here is that
    device is often used as a stand-in for age — so we measured whether it works as one.
    It does not.
  </p>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>The overall split</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>What we counted</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Acts measured</td><td>{수(셈.잰팀수)} of {수(셈.던진팀수)}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Reads in the window</td><td>{수(셈.전체합)}</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Desktop, all reading added together</td><td><b>{몫(셈.합쳐본데스크톱몫)}</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Desktop for the median act</td><td><b>{몫(셈.데스크톱몫중앙값)}</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Spread across debut decades, median act (points)</td><td><b>{띠폭 == null ? "not measured" : (Number(띠폭) * 100).toFixed(1)}</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Phone (mobile web plus app)</td><td>{몫(1 - Number(셈.합쳐본데스크톱몫))}</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      Two numbers, not one, because they answer different questions. Added together, the
      most-read acts dominate the total; the median act tells you about a typical act. That
      they differ by {점(Number(셈.데스크톱몫중앙값) - Number(셈.합쳐본데스크톱몫))} means the
      very biggest acts sit slightly further toward the phone than the rest.
      {' '}{수(셈.뺀팀수)} acts were dropped rather than shown — {d.선.바닥선.toLocaleString('en-US')}
      {' '}reads in the window is our floor, because below it a percentage moves on a handful
      of visits.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>It does not move with debut era</h2>
    <p>
      If device tracked the age of an audience at all, acts that debuted in the 1990s ought
      to be read differently from acts that debuted in the 2020s. Here is every ten-year band
      that holds at least ten acts.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Founded</th><th>Acts</th><th>Desktop share, median act</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {볼띠.map((b) => (
          <tr><td>{b.띠}</td><td>{b.팀수}</td><td>{몫(b.데스크톱몫중앙값)}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      The whole spread is{' '}<b>{점(띠폭)}</b>{' '}— from {가장낮은띠 && 가장낮은띠.띠} at
      {' '}{가장낮은띠 && 몫(가장낮은띠.데스크톱몫중앙값)} to {가장높은띠 && 가장높은띠.띠} at
      {' '}{가장높은띠 && 몫(가장높은띠.데스크톱몫중앙값)}. Across roughly three decades of
      debuts, that is flat.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      {작은띠.length > 0 && (
        <>Bands with fewer than ten acts are left out of the table rather than shown as a
        percentage: {작은띠.map((b) => `${b.띠} (${b.팀수})`).join(', ')}. </>
      )}
      {수(셈.띠없는팀수)} acts have no founding year recorded in Wikidata; they are in the
      totals above but in no band.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>And it stays flat when we drop the small acts</h2>
    <p>
      A percentage of a small number is a fragile thing, so we ran the same comparison using
      only acts read at least {수(많이읽힌선)} times in the window —
      {' '}{수(많이읽힌.length)} of them. If the flatness above were an artefact of noisy
      small acts, it would break here.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Founded</th><th>Acts</th><th>Desktop share, median act</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {많이읽힌띠.map((x) => (
          <tr><td>{x.띠}</td><td>{x.팀수}</td><td>{몫(x.중앙)}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="note">
      Median across all {수(많이읽힌.length)} well-read acts: {몫(많이읽힌중앙)}. Spread
      between the bands: {점(많이읽힌폭)}. It does not break. Bands under five acts are not
      shown.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where the extremes are, and why we are not making them the story</h2>
    <p>
      Individual acts do sit far apart. We are printing the ends of the list because hiding
      them would be worse, but read the reads column: the extremes are mostly acts with small
      totals, where a share swings easily.
    </p>
    <h3>Read most on desktop</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Act</th><th>Founded</th><th>Reads</th><th>Desktop</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {d.데스크톱쪽스물.slice(0, 10).map((t) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={위키(t.제목)} rel="nofollow">{t.이름}</a></td>
            <td>{t.데뷔해 ?? '—'}</td>
            <td>{수(t.전체)}</td>
            <td>{몫(t.데스크톱몫)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h3>Read most on a phone</h3>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Act</th><th>Founded</th><th>Reads</th><th>Desktop</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {d.전화쪽스물.slice(0, 10).map((t) => (
          <tr>
            <td><a href={위키(t.제목)} rel="nofollow">{t.이름}</a></td>
            <td>{t.데뷔해 ?? '—'}</td>
            <td>{수(t.전체)}</td>
            <td>{몫(t.데스크톱몫)}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>The arithmetic checks against yesterday's count</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Desktop share is desktop reads divided by all-access reads, so it is only right if the
      denominator is right. We already had all-access totals for these acts, collected
      separately for{' '}<a href="/member-vs-group">the member-versus-group
      count</a>. Fetching all-access again today and comparing:
      {' '}<b>{d.검산.한푼이하} of {d.검산.견준팀수}</b>{' '}acts agree to within one percent, and
      the median difference is {몫(d.검산.중앙어긋남)}. That is what we wanted to see — the
      well has not moved under us, and the two counts are the same measurement.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>🔴 What this does not say</h2>
    {d.이것이아닌것.map((l) => <p class="note">{l}</p>)}
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where else this leads</h2>
    <p class="note">
      For who is reading rather than on what,
      {' '}<a href="/what-countries-read">we counted by country</a>{' '}— and found, among other
      things, that five Latin American countries returned no Korean article at all in a
      fortnight. For how unevenly the reading is spread across acts,
      {' '}<a href="/attention-share">24 acts of 774 hold half of it</a>. For whether the
      generation labels the press uses show up in reading at all,
      {' '}<a href="/generations">they do not sit where the reading breaks</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/desktop-or-phone" />

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    {d.우물.map((l) => <p class="note">{l}</p>)}
    <p class="note">Collected {d.잰때}.</p>
  </section>
</WikiTip>
